WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.659 --> 00:00:05.490
On this day, exactly a 100 years ago the Paris
peace treaty of Saint Germain dealing with

00:00:05.490 --> 00:00:10.070
the breakup of the Austrian part of the Austro-Hungairan
empire came into effect.

00:00:10.070 --> 00:00:13.879
Before watching this video I suggest you go
watch my previous video about the final days

00:00:13.879 --> 00:00:14.879
of Austria-Hungary.

00:00:14.879 --> 00:00:15.879
Anyways.

00:00:15.879 --> 00:00:20.050
As you know the Austro-Hungarian empire was
divided into two main parts, the Austrian

00:00:20.050 --> 00:00:21.130
and the Hungarian.

00:00:21.130 --> 00:00:25.570
As such at the end of WW1 there were two separate
Paris Peace Treaties dealing with the two

00:00:25.570 --> 00:00:27.349
separate parts of the empire.

00:00:27.349 --> 00:00:31.640
Today we’re going to look at the immediate
post war history of the Austrian part of the

00:00:31.640 --> 00:00:35.390
Empire and the peace treaty dealing with it,
the Treaty of Saint Germain.

00:00:35.390 --> 00:00:39.500
However before we look at anything specific,
this map needs to be addressed.

00:00:39.500 --> 00:00:43.719
It is a map showing the ethnic makeup of the
Austrian half of the empire and therefore

00:00:43.719 --> 00:00:47.649
it is very important to understand because
many of the underlying issues talked about

00:00:47.649 --> 00:00:50.699
in this video revolve around ethnic issues.

00:00:50.699 --> 00:00:54.430
The problem is this map which is oftentimes
shown when talking about post war Austria

00:00:54.430 --> 00:00:58.570
Hungary does not necessarily show the ethnic
makeup of the Empire.

00:00:58.570 --> 00:00:59.570
Let me explain.

00:00:59.570 --> 00:01:04.110
This map and others like it are based off
of the 1910 Austro-Hungarian census.

00:01:04.110 --> 00:01:08.230
Side note here this census was conducted a
bit differently by the two separate political

00:01:08.230 --> 00:01:12.930
entities of the empire and today I will talk
only about the Austrian census not the Hungarian

00:01:12.930 --> 00:01:13.930
one.

00:01:13.930 --> 00:01:17.520
The first thing that needs to be addressed
about this census is that just because a province

00:01:17.520 --> 00:01:21.760
on the map is showing let's say Polish as
a majority that doesn’t mean it was the

00:01:21.760 --> 00:01:23.720
only ethnicity living there.

00:01:23.720 --> 00:01:29.220
A more accurate representation would be this,
and yes I made the map myself and i know it’s

00:01:29.220 --> 00:01:32.670
not perfect but it will have to do as it took
me like a week to make.

00:01:32.670 --> 00:01:37.870
Anyways so whenever you see a map like this
keep in mind it only shows the majority ethnicity

00:01:37.870 --> 00:01:40.160
of a province not the whole population.

00:01:40.160 --> 00:01:45.580
Second, the Austrian census never asked for
a person's ethnicity outright; it only asked

00:01:45.580 --> 00:01:50.400
for a person's “Umgangssprache” which
translates into something like everyday spoken

00:01:50.400 --> 00:01:51.400
language.

00:01:51.400 --> 00:01:56.270
Meaning what the census actually recorded
was a person's most spoken everyday language.

00:01:56.270 --> 00:02:01.150
Therefore this map does not show ethnic divisions
but language divisions, which even though

00:02:01.150 --> 00:02:05.660
are very heavily correlated with ethnic divisions
aren’t the same thing.

00:02:05.660 --> 00:02:10.340
For example it was completely common for people
who lived in the border regions and identified

00:02:10.340 --> 00:02:14.950
as Czechs to use mainly German as that was
the language at work or even at large social

00:02:14.950 --> 00:02:15.950
gatherings.

00:02:15.950 --> 00:02:19.610
And these kinds of people would be identified
as Austrian-Germans in the census and on this

00:02:19.610 --> 00:02:20.610
map.

00:02:20.610 --> 00:02:24.570
Therefore it has to be stated that due to
this reason Austrian-Germans are over-reported

00:02:24.570 --> 00:02:29.380
in the 1910 census and subsequently also in
the map created from the census.

00:02:29.380 --> 00:02:33.920
However, this is not to say the census and
the map is completely wrong, specially because

00:02:33.920 --> 00:02:38.980
when adjusted for post war migrations it is
very similar to the censuses conducted after

00:02:38.980 --> 00:02:39.980
the war.

00:02:39.980 --> 00:02:43.590
But also from these comparisons it becomes
clear that Austrian-Germans were in fact over

00:02:43.590 --> 00:02:48.620
reported in the 1910 census but not by some
huge margin as some nationalists would have

00:02:48.620 --> 00:02:49.620
you believe.

00:02:49.620 --> 00:02:54.680
So when looking at this map keep in mind it
is a map showing the most spoken self identified

00:02:54.680 --> 00:02:59.680
language in an area not the majority ethnicity
in an area even though those two things are

00:02:59.680 --> 00:03:01.400
very heavily correlated.

00:03:01.400 --> 00:03:05.900
Now when it came to the Paris peace conference
in 1919 Austria was for the most part at the

00:03:05.900 --> 00:03:07.870
start completely ignored.

00:03:07.870 --> 00:03:12.000
With the entente being heavily preoccupied
drafting a peace treaty for Germany as it

00:03:12.000 --> 00:03:15.350
was seen by the allies as the largest future
threat.

00:03:15.350 --> 00:03:19.220
Therefore the Austrian delegates at the start
of the peace talks struggled to even get a

00:03:19.220 --> 00:03:21.350
meeting with the allied council.

00:03:21.350 --> 00:03:25.380
Eventually they were assigned their own council
and a draft of a peace treaty was made for

00:03:25.380 --> 00:03:30.000
Austria, a draft in which Austria had very
little say in but such were the peace negotiation

00:03:30.000 --> 00:03:32.690
for any losing power in the Paris Peace Conference.

00:03:32.690 --> 00:03:37.360
As it stood the main points of what was to
become the Treaty of Saint Germain where.

00:03:37.360 --> 00:03:42.000
Austria losing all of its non-core land including
the German majority in Bohemia.

00:03:42.000 --> 00:03:46.380
Austria having to pay war reparations but
these were actually never truly defined and

00:03:46.380 --> 00:03:50.410
later kind of forgotten about on purpose because
Austria didn’t really have the post war

00:03:50.410 --> 00:03:52.620
economy to pay for them anyways.

00:03:52.620 --> 00:03:56.690
The successor states had the right to seize
all state property of the former Empire which

00:03:56.690 --> 00:03:58.660
lies within their border.

00:03:58.660 --> 00:04:02.560
All succer states will be held accountable
to hold a percentage of the former Empires

00:04:02.560 --> 00:04:04.480
debt as defined by the allies.

00:04:04.480 --> 00:04:09.319
There will be a plebiscite held in the province
of Carinthia which got taken over by Yugoslav

00:04:09.319 --> 00:04:13.160
forces during the confusing mess which was
the breakup of Austria-Hungary.

00:04:13.160 --> 00:04:19.090
The German majority Burgenland which is currently
held by Hungary will be given to Austria.

00:04:19.090 --> 00:04:23.250
German Austria is to renounce all claims to
the German majority lands of the former Empire

00:04:23.250 --> 00:04:28.280
and to symbolize this change its name to just
Austria, also it is not allowed under any

00:04:28.280 --> 00:04:32.210
circumstances to unite with Germany at any
point in the future.

00:04:32.210 --> 00:04:37.200
Of course there were many more points of the
Saint Germain treaty than I have stated, 376

00:04:37.200 --> 00:04:40.180
more points to be exact but there’s no time
to mention them all.

00:04:40.180 --> 00:04:45.210
The Peace Treaty of Saint Germain was concluded
and begrudgingly signed by the Austrians 10th

00:04:45.210 --> 00:04:47.300
of September 1919.

00:04:47.300 --> 00:04:51.311
However while all these negotiations were
happening in Paris life didn’t just stop

00:04:51.311 --> 00:04:56.130
in the former lands of the Empire and in fact
it became in many ways even more chaotic than

00:04:56.130 --> 00:04:57.520
it already was.

00:04:57.520 --> 00:05:02.410
For example when Czechoslovakia was proclaimed
on October 28th, the German population living

00:05:02.410 --> 00:05:06.240
in the lands of the Bohemian crown declared
their own independence.

00:05:06.240 --> 00:05:11.100
Quickly establishing their own governing bodies
and proclaiming loyalty to the Austrian German

00:05:11.100 --> 00:05:14.810
government in Vienna not the Czechoslovak
government in Prague.

00:05:14.810 --> 00:05:19.500
Austria however was in no military position
to defend these lands and since Czechoslovakia

00:05:19.500 --> 00:05:23.740
declared possession over all the lands of
the Bohemian crown regardless of the German

00:05:23.740 --> 00:05:27.220
population they started occupying these lands
by force.

00:05:27.220 --> 00:05:31.190
With Czechoslovakia being in control of all
the land later to be called the Sudetenland

00:05:31.190 --> 00:05:32.190
by the start of 1919.

00:05:32.190 --> 00:05:33.340
Just in time to begin a war with Poland.

00:05:33.340 --> 00:05:37.830
Remember Tesin in Silesia and how two different
governing Polish and Czech bodies were established

00:05:37.830 --> 00:05:41.250
and then came together in a tenues demarcation
agreement.

00:05:41.250 --> 00:05:45.410
Part of that agreement was that no sovereign
rule was to be conducted in the area until

00:05:45.410 --> 00:05:48.010
a concrete border was agreed upon in Paris.

00:05:48.010 --> 00:05:51.860
Well that was the Czechoslovak interpretation
of the agreement anyways.

00:05:51.860 --> 00:05:55.680
But this agreement was then broken by the
Poles who started preparing for parliamentary

00:05:55.680 --> 00:06:01.740
elections in the area which was seen by Czechoslovakia
as a motion of “sovereign rule” over Tesin.

00:06:01.740 --> 00:06:05.430
Therefore Czechoslovakia protested to this,
the Poles disagreed on the interpretation

00:06:05.430 --> 00:06:10.070
of the agreement saying this didn’t apply
and so the stage was set for a war in late

00:06:10.070 --> 00:06:11.160
January 1919.

00:06:11.160 --> 00:06:16.120
Why was Tesin so important to both sides,
well because not only was it a very important

00:06:16.120 --> 00:06:21.020
train hub in central Europe which was a big
deal in 1919 but it also had very large coal

00:06:21.020 --> 00:06:24.930
mines and steel industry that both of the
infant countries needed to strengthen their

00:06:24.930 --> 00:06:26.330
economic position.

00:06:26.330 --> 00:06:30.350
On top of that Czechoslovakia had a further
reason why not to give up Tesin and that was

00:06:30.350 --> 00:06:34.250
because it was part of the Bohemian crown
lands with a Polish majority.

00:06:34.250 --> 00:06:38.229
This meant that if part of the Bohemian Crown
lands with a Polish majority was to be given

00:06:38.229 --> 00:06:42.290
to Poland who’s to say that the Bohemian
Crown lands with German majority can’t be

00:06:42.290 --> 00:06:43.830
given to Austria.

00:06:43.830 --> 00:06:48.680
It would set a dangerous precedent that Czechoslovakia
was actively trying to avoid.

00:06:48.680 --> 00:06:52.840
This is why on January 23rd when Czechoslovakia
knew it had the upper military hand since

00:06:52.840 --> 00:06:57.550
Poland was fighting German, and West Ukraninan
border disputes invaded the Polish side of

00:06:57.550 --> 00:06:58.550
Tesin.

00:06:58.550 --> 00:07:03.669
After 7 days of mostly very one-sided fighting
and strong diplomatic pressure from the Allies

00:07:03.669 --> 00:07:08.150
a ceasefire was reached, with Czechoslovakia
now in control of almost all of Tesin economic

00:07:08.150 --> 00:07:09.240
production.

00:07:09.240 --> 00:07:14.290
What followed next was more than a year of
negotiations during which Czechoslovakia dragged

00:07:14.290 --> 00:07:19.930
their feet at every possible moment, this
was begrudgingly tolerated by the allies mostly

00:07:19.930 --> 00:07:24.190
due to their more negative view of Poland
after certain events in Lviv that we will

00:07:24.190 --> 00:07:25.360
get to soon.

00:07:25.360 --> 00:07:29.320
However eventually an agreement was reached
in July 1920 where Czechoslovakia was allowed

00:07:29.320 --> 00:07:34.750
to retain control of the economica/strategically
important areas of Tesin, and Poland was given

00:07:34.750 --> 00:07:37.199
Polish majority lands in Spis and Orava.

00:07:37.199 --> 00:07:42.220
This was later accompanied by another agreement
in 1924 that exchanged yet again a few towns

00:07:42.220 --> 00:07:43.810
between the two countries.

00:07:43.810 --> 00:07:48.690
Skipping from that to probably the most chaotic
area of the former Empire, the now self proclaimed

00:07:48.690 --> 00:07:50.920
West Ukranians People’s Republic.

00:07:50.920 --> 00:07:55.300
When this republic was proclaimed on the first
of November 1918 it was done so because the

00:07:55.300 --> 00:07:59.639
majority Ukranian population of Eastern Galicia
feared that they would become subject to the

00:07:59.639 --> 00:08:04.759
New Polish Republic and these fears were not
unfounded as both the Polish Liquidation committee

00:08:04.759 --> 00:08:09.380
and the Polish republic made their intentions
of annexing whole of Austrian Galicia very

00:08:09.380 --> 00:08:10.380
clear.

00:08:10.380 --> 00:08:14.280
The WUPR early on saw a lot of support from
the local population and was able to raise

00:08:14.280 --> 00:08:19.479
an army of almost 100 thousands man which
thanks to raiding of abandoned weapons warehouses

00:08:19.479 --> 00:08:23.229
left behind by the Austro-Hungarian military
was very well equipped.

00:08:23.229 --> 00:08:29.000
The army also included a lot of veterans of
the great war so by November 1918 WUPR had

00:08:29.000 --> 00:08:33.829
a large, well equipped, and well trained army
to be able to withstand not just Poland but

00:08:33.829 --> 00:08:37.429
also conduct its own expeditions into Bukovina
and Ruthenia, these were however meat with

00:08:37.429 --> 00:08:38.429
very little success.

00:08:38.429 --> 00:08:42.619
The WUPR also symbolically unified with their
sister country in the former Russian Empire

00:08:42.619 --> 00:08:46.410
and somewhat helped with fighting against
the bolsheviks and white Russians but this

00:08:46.410 --> 00:08:51.420
unification was only on paper as both countries
continued acting as independent political

00:08:51.420 --> 00:08:52.420
entities.

00:08:52.420 --> 00:08:57.420
Plus WUPR was actually very different to the
Ukraninan People’s Republic as unlike them

00:08:57.420 --> 00:09:02.329
they had an actively well working bureaucratic
system even during this chaotic time which

00:09:02.329 --> 00:09:07.309
they inherited from Austria-Hungary not to
mention the WUPR’s much better trained and

00:09:07.309 --> 00:09:08.740
equipped army.

00:09:08.740 --> 00:09:12.570
But coming back to the conflict at hand to
understand the Polish interests in Eastern

00:09:12.570 --> 00:09:17.540
Galicia we have to look at the primary language
map, as you can see even though Ukranian is

00:09:17.540 --> 00:09:21.920
the majority language in the lands claimed
by the WUPR there is a very sizable polish

00:09:21.920 --> 00:09:27.809
presence with Lviv and the surrounding area
even having a Polish majority, and so when

00:09:27.809 --> 00:09:31.790
West Ukranian troops took over Lviv in early
November it was meat with a strong Polish

00:09:31.790 --> 00:09:36.459
resistance that along with the help from Poland
itself managed to retake Lviv by the end of

00:09:36.459 --> 00:09:37.649
the month.

00:09:37.649 --> 00:09:42.000
After that the Polish troops in the city along
with its Polish inhabitants attacked much

00:09:42.000 --> 00:09:46.740
of the jewish community of Lviv blaming them
for many of the unfortunate events currently

00:09:46.740 --> 00:09:48.189
happening in central Europe.

00:09:48.189 --> 00:09:52.819
How many people died during this attack depends
on who you ask but most historians give the

00:09:52.819 --> 00:09:57.980
number of around a 100 people, what was however
more devastating in the long run was the looting

00:09:57.980 --> 00:09:59.910
that accompanied the killings.

00:09:59.910 --> 00:10:05.730
Around 11.4 million crowns (or about 15 to
20 million dollars in today's money) worth

00:10:05.730 --> 00:10:09.660
of wealth was destroyed or looted from Jewish
business.

00:10:09.660 --> 00:10:14.129
This pogrom was widely reported in the western
papers including the New York times and was

00:10:14.129 --> 00:10:19.959
a very large instigator in Western distrust
of the Polish campaigns, remember the Tesin

00:10:19.959 --> 00:10:24.929
negotiations, anyways, therefore the Allies
became more favorable towards the WUPR the

00:10:24.929 --> 00:10:27.499
following months in early 1919.

00:10:27.499 --> 00:10:32.220
For the next few months West Ukraniane troops
laid siege to Lviv but were never fully able

00:10:32.220 --> 00:10:36.470
to retake it, however, they did see some success
on the Polish front as a whole, and due to

00:10:36.470 --> 00:10:41.779
this and also heavy allied diplomatic involvement
a ceasefire was reached between Poland and

00:10:41.779 --> 00:10:45.129
the WUPR on the 25th of February 1919.

00:10:45.129 --> 00:10:50.480
After that a series of very complicated negotiations
took place, the result of which is best described

00:10:50.480 --> 00:10:57.639
by an allied ambassador presenting an armistice
Treaty to the WUPR on the 30th of February.

00:10:57.639 --> 00:11:03.620
"Today, your military situation is good, but
it may soon change to your disadvantage.

00:11:03.620 --> 00:11:08.410
Poland and Czechoslovakia have signed an armistice,
enabling the Poles to transport ammunition

00:11:08.410 --> 00:11:10.110
over Czech territory.

00:11:10.110 --> 00:11:14.220
An armistice agreement will also be reached
soon between Poland and Germany.

00:11:14.220 --> 00:11:18.309
The Bolsheviks have not as yet entered Polish
territory, and the Poles, therefore, are not

00:11:18.309 --> 00:11:21.040
constrained to send an army against them.

00:11:21.040 --> 00:11:24.850
Realizing this, the Poles are strengthened
and encouraged.

00:11:24.850 --> 00:11:29.860
If our proposal is not accepted by you, the
whole Entente will hold you responsible.

00:11:29.860 --> 00:11:34.230
On one side you will be at war with Poland,
which will have the support of General Haller's

00:11:34.230 --> 00:11:35.929
well-organized six divisions.

00:11:35.929 --> 00:11:40.709
While on your other side, the Bolsheviks,
having already taken Kiev and a major portion

00:11:40.709 --> 00:11:43.980
of your territories, are advancing relentlessly
upon you.

00:11:43.980 --> 00:11:50.019
If, however, you accept our proposal, all
efforts will be made to recognize your independence.

00:11:50.019 --> 00:11:55.399
The very fact that we are negotiating with
you by putting forward this proposal, is,

00:11:55.399 --> 00:12:01.040
to a certain extent, proof of our recognition
of your State; one does not negotiate with

00:12:01.040 --> 00:12:03.389
something that does not exist.

00:12:03.389 --> 00:12:08.049
With our help, you will defeat the Bolsheviks,
regain your lost territories, and will not

00:12:08.049 --> 00:12:12.600
come empty-handed to the Peace Conference
... Steps are being taken to include your

00:12:12.600 --> 00:12:17.639
representatives at the Peace Conference, and
a diplomatic mission will be sent to you which

00:12:17.639 --> 00:12:21.339
will keep our countries informed of your needs.

00:12:21.339 --> 00:12:25.299
Remember the proverb: 'Heaven helps those
who help themselves.'

00:12:25.299 --> 00:12:28.750
For you, the Entente represents this heaven.

00:12:28.750 --> 00:12:34.589
Your decision could mean the beginning of
a new existence and national independence.

00:12:34.589 --> 00:12:39.480
Never and nowhere will you have an opportunity
such as this again.

00:12:39.480 --> 00:12:42.139
It is a great and solemn moment.

00:12:42.139 --> 00:12:47.299
The future of your nation is in your hands."

00:12:47.299 --> 00:12:51.999
Among other things the armistice treaty defined
the division between the two countries with

00:12:51.999 --> 00:12:57.480
Poland taking control of Lviv and the very
important oil fields south of the city, however,

00:12:57.480 --> 00:13:03.489
any oil/revenue gotten from the oil fields
will be equally divided between the WUPR and

00:13:03.489 --> 00:13:04.489
Poland.

00:13:04.489 --> 00:13:08.429
The WUPR commanders after some heavy debating
decided they didn’t want to give up the

00:13:08.429 --> 00:13:12.860
territory they already controlled nor the
very important city of Lviv and so refused

00:13:12.860 --> 00:13:15.820
the treaty and canceled the ceasefire the
following March.

00:13:15.820 --> 00:13:21.060
As pointed out by the allied ambassador Poland
was now more than capable of defeating the

00:13:21.060 --> 00:13:28.550
WUPR which they did a couple of months later
with the WUPR ceasing to exist mid July 1919.

00:13:28.550 --> 00:13:32.610
Skipping over from there we’ll now look
at the southern lands of Austria.

00:13:32.610 --> 00:13:33.649
First Carinthia.

00:13:33.649 --> 00:13:38.329
Here Austrians and Slovenians with some support
from Serbian volunteers have been in a conflict

00:13:38.329 --> 00:13:39.509
since October.

00:13:39.509 --> 00:13:43.480
This was because the area of Carinthia had
a mixed population with a German majority

00:13:43.480 --> 00:13:48.629
as a whole but with southern provinces having
a Slovenian majority when taken individually.

00:13:48.629 --> 00:13:52.819
Naturally during the break up of the Empire
multiple councils were established either

00:13:52.819 --> 00:13:55.339
proclaiming loyalty to Vienna or Ljubljana.

00:13:55.339 --> 00:14:00.820
The two sides eventually came to a demarcation
agreement and in November 1918 the Slovenian

00:14:00.820 --> 00:14:05.879
general Rudolf Maister started occupying the
towns agreed upon as being under Slovenian

00:14:05.879 --> 00:14:06.879
control.

00:14:06.879 --> 00:14:10.360
However, disagreements over the interpretation
of the demarcation lines came by the end of

00:14:10.360 --> 00:14:15.339
the month as Maister captured Völkermarkt,
a town that Austrians argued wasn’t included

00:14:15.339 --> 00:14:16.769
in the agreement.

00:14:16.769 --> 00:14:22.439
As such tensions rose and by the time of January
1919 the simple occupation of their respective

00:14:22.439 --> 00:14:27.089
demarcation lines turned into an all out war
between the two countries.

00:14:27.089 --> 00:14:30.670
Slovenian troops emerged having the upper
hand and even started planning an attack on

00:14:30.670 --> 00:14:36.060
Klagenfurt in february but by that time a
ceasefire was negotiated due to pressure from

00:14:36.060 --> 00:14:37.060
the allies.

00:14:37.060 --> 00:14:41.149
The allies, after inspecting the situation
in the area, decided a plebiscite will be

00:14:41.149 --> 00:14:44.989
held which included some of the towns that
were agreed to be in Slovenian possession

00:14:44.989 --> 00:14:47.019
in the first demarcation agreement.

00:14:47.019 --> 00:14:51.459
This was unacceptable for the Slovenians as
they knew if a plebiscite was held taking

00:14:51.459 --> 00:14:54.369
the entire region as a whole they weren’t
going to win.

00:14:54.369 --> 00:14:59.149
So at the end of April they broke the ceasefire
and launched a full scale offensive.

00:14:59.149 --> 00:15:03.429
This proved not so successful and Austrian
troops actually managed to push the Slovenian

00:15:03.429 --> 00:15:07.759
forces all the way back to Slovenia where
they were stopped by Yugoslav forces that

00:15:07.759 --> 00:15:09.589
came to reinforce the front.

00:15:09.589 --> 00:15:14.019
More Yugoslav troops came the following month
and with their help another Slovenian offensive

00:15:14.019 --> 00:15:18.649
was launched which by early June captured
much of the Klagenfurt basin, this was however

00:15:18.649 --> 00:15:24.119
for naught as the Allies now fed up with all
the fighting issued an ultimatum to Yugoslavia

00:15:24.119 --> 00:15:28.269
to withdraw from the area so a plebiscite
can be held or else.

00:15:28.269 --> 00:15:32.459
Yugoslav troops reluctantly withdrew and the
plebiscite results showed that 60% of the

00:15:32.459 --> 00:15:37.310
population wanted to remain with Austria,
what is however interesting is that half of

00:15:37.310 --> 00:15:42.230
the Sloevnian population in the area voted
to remain with Austria as they saw themself

00:15:42.230 --> 00:15:45.379
having stronger ties to the Austria than to
Yugoslavia.

00:15:45.379 --> 00:15:50.019
Therefore, outside of a few border towns that
were agreed to be given to Slovenia, Carinthia

00:15:50.019 --> 00:15:52.410
as a whole remained in Austrian possession.

00:15:52.410 --> 00:15:57.170
Then there's the adriatic question or the
adriatic problem which was the struggle between

00:15:57.170 --> 00:16:01.379
the newly formed Yugoslavia and the Kingdom
of Italy over the former Austrian Adriatic

00:16:01.379 --> 00:16:02.379
coast.

00:16:02.379 --> 00:16:07.069
The allies agreed to give all of this land
to Italy during the 1915 London agreement

00:16:07.069 --> 00:16:08.829
which brought it into the war.

00:16:08.829 --> 00:16:13.620
However, as Austria-Hungary fell apart and
minorities within the country started claiming

00:16:13.620 --> 00:16:17.430
land, the Adriatic coast was claimed first
by the state of Slovenes, Croats and Serbs

00:16:17.430 --> 00:16:22.269
and later Yugoslavia and considering that
outside of western Istria all of this land

00:16:22.269 --> 00:16:27.079
had a Yugoslav ethnic majority the rest of
the allies started to backtrack on their promises

00:16:27.079 --> 00:16:28.079
to Italy.

00:16:28.079 --> 00:16:31.959
They did give Italy Austrian majority south
tyrol but this was different since Austria

00:16:31.959 --> 00:16:36.339
was the enemy and it was easier to swallow
giving a majority Austrian land away than

00:16:36.339 --> 00:16:39.980
Yugoslav land because Yugoslavia was part
of the allies.

00:16:39.980 --> 00:16:44.100
Not to mention the post war campaign of the
USA for self determination.

00:16:44.100 --> 00:16:48.959
The Paris peace talks were then further complicated
by the fact that Yugoslav forces and civilians

00:16:48.959 --> 00:16:53.790
clashed with the Italian army occupying the
Adriatic coast, leading mostly America but

00:16:53.790 --> 00:16:58.149
also Britain and France to send occupation
forces of their own to the area to try to

00:16:58.149 --> 00:16:59.660
ease the tensions.

00:16:59.660 --> 00:17:03.899
Many proposals and counter proposals were
made but none of the two countries could agree

00:17:03.899 --> 00:17:08.190
on anything and the rest of the allies became
increasingly irritated with the talks going

00:17:08.190 --> 00:17:12.650
nowhere considering they had their hands full
with other large problems happening all over

00:17:12.650 --> 00:17:16.750
the former Empire, plus while the talks where
going nowhere the clashes between the two

00:17:16.750 --> 00:17:19.170
countries continued to increase.

00:17:19.170 --> 00:17:24.190
In the end 12th of November 1920 Treaty of
Rapallo was signed between the two countries

00:17:24.190 --> 00:17:28.670
ending the dispute over the Adriatic coastline,
which now looked like this.

00:17:28.670 --> 00:17:33.490
In the treaty the city of Fiume would become
independent but it was later given to Italy

00:17:33.490 --> 00:17:35.800
under the Treaty of Rome in 1924.

00:17:35.800 --> 00:17:40.190
The Italians viewed this entire situation
as a backstab by the allies who promised them

00:17:40.190 --> 00:17:45.630
everything in the London agreement only to
not help them during the actual peace talks,

00:17:45.630 --> 00:17:49.610
resulting in Italy having to sign a treaty
which didn’t give them as much land as they

00:17:49.610 --> 00:17:51.240
wanted.

00:17:51.240 --> 00:17:55.810
Lastly we’ll look at Burgenland, this area
was part of the Hungarian kingdom but had

00:17:55.810 --> 00:17:57.940
a German speaking majority.

00:17:57.940 --> 00:18:01.980
Therefore in the treaty of Saint Germain it
was decided to be given to Austria, however,

00:18:01.980 --> 00:18:06.860
this had to be postponed as Hungary was having
a thing which we’ll touch upon in my next

00:18:06.860 --> 00:18:07.860
video.

00:18:07.860 --> 00:18:11.950
Once Horthy came into power and Hungary was
again cooperating with the allies, the transition

00:18:11.950 --> 00:18:15.260
of Burgenland was set for August 1921.

00:18:15.260 --> 00:18:20.240
But Hungarians and Coratians in the area around
Sopron created a militia to fight the Austrians

00:18:20.240 --> 00:18:24.570
because they didn’t want to be part of Austria,
after repulsing the Austrians they declared

00:18:24.570 --> 00:18:26.730
their own republic, the Lajtabánság.

00:18:26.730 --> 00:18:30.580
The Hungarian government couldn’t do anything
about this as under the allied treaties they

00:18:30.580 --> 00:18:34.390
had to withdraw their troops from the area
and the Austrians were unable to defeat the

00:18:34.390 --> 00:18:39.060
scrapy militia who employed very successful
guerilla tactics against them.

00:18:39.060 --> 00:18:43.560
So Austrians started negotiations with the
Hungarians to figure out what to do next,

00:18:43.560 --> 00:18:46.760
all while Lajtabánság acted as its own country.

00:18:46.760 --> 00:18:50.890
Trains going through it had to pay dues, they
printed their own stamps and even had their

00:18:50.890 --> 00:18:51.970
own elections.

00:18:51.970 --> 00:18:56.340
From these elections the people decided they
wanted to be a monarchy, however, a split

00:18:56.340 --> 00:19:00.280
between who should be the monarch happened
and the state started to fall apart on its

00:19:00.280 --> 00:19:01.280
own.

00:19:01.280 --> 00:19:04.190
Meanwhile Austria and Hungary reached an agreement
on what to do.

00:19:04.190 --> 00:19:08.970
Hungary will help Austria occupy the new country
which now was much easier as Lajtabánság

00:19:08.970 --> 00:19:13.630
was falling apart, all while a plebiscite
will be held in the Sopron area as this was

00:19:13.630 --> 00:19:17.701
the main area which had a sizeable Croatian
and Hungarian population that didn’t want

00:19:17.701 --> 00:19:18.860
to join Austria.

00:19:18.860 --> 00:19:24.400
In December 1921 Sopron voted to stay with
Hungary while the rest of Burgenland joined

00:19:24.400 --> 00:19:25.800
Austria.

00:19:25.800 --> 00:19:29.280
This is where I will conclude the video about
the Treaty of Saint Germain and the lands

00:19:29.280 --> 00:19:30.280
it dealt with.

00:19:30.280 --> 00:19:34.580
Obviously I couldn’t talk about everything
like for example the post war state of Austria

00:19:34.580 --> 00:19:37.530
itself, because this video can’t go on forever.

00:19:37.530 --> 00:19:41.730
However, I will give a more general overview
ending of the break of the entire Empire in

00:19:41.730 --> 00:19:45.560
my treaty of Trianon video coming out on the
31st of July so if you don’t want to miss

00:19:45.560 --> 00:19:47.630
that subscribe and hit the bell icon.

